  "notes": "Winton Avenue runs along the plate's left edge (west side cut off), so its crossings are given as T. Street stub north off Epworth at x 742 is lettered 'Bu...' (name cut by plate edge) = '?'. The 40 ft north-south avenue at x 808 (South Circle to Keenan) is lettered only 'AVE.' there; it lines up with Station Avenue named south of the railroad, so named Station Avenue. At South Circle/Darrow (1160,2228) the street continuing north is Circle Avenue, whose roadway also curves south-west into South Circle Avenue. Mellwood '?' at (1545,2812): Mellwood ends where an avenue lettered only 'AVE.' runs off north-east (angle point / name change). The 50 ft east-west street at y 4465 between Station and Platt Avenues has no printed name ('?'). Evens Avenue (y about 4180) is printed as vacated: not picked. Railroad crosses Station Avenue just south of Keenan."
